A vast server room landscape rendered in Piet Mondrian's distinctive neoplasticism style, with towering server racks abstracted into bold rectangular blocks of primary red, yellow, and blue separated by thick black grid lines. The composition shows 60% of the blocks in warm orange and red tones dominating the upper and central canvas, while 40% in cooler blue tones occupy a smaller corner section. The geometric forms create a dynamic sense of imbalance and shifting power, with the larger colored sections appearing to expand and push against the smaller ones. Clean white spaces punctuate the composition, creating rhythm and breathing room between the stark color fields. The perspective suggests depth through overlapping planes, evoking endless rows of digital infrastructure reduced to pure form and color.
